 "result": "Call order (this repo is `tessel`, with renamed Flask-style internals):\n\n1. `Tessel.finalize_request` (`src/tessel/app.py:1021`). It's called from the dispatch method at line 1019, and from the error handler at line 948. It calls `make_response` (`app.py:1224`) to build the `Response`.\n2. `Tessel.finalize_reply` (`src/tessel/app.py:1394`). It runs the after-request functions, then persists the session at lines 1415–1416. It skips this if `is_null_session` is true.\n3. `SessionInterface.persist_session` (`src/tessel/sessions.py:263`). This is the abstract hook. The default implementation is `SignedCookieSessionInterface.persist_session` (`sessions.py:337`), set as `session_interface` at `app.py:250`.\n4. Inside `SignedCookieSessionInterface.persist_session`:\n   - It first reads the cookie settings from the `get_cookie_*` helpers.\n   - If the session was modified and is now empty, it calls `response.delete_cookie` (`sessions.py:356`).\n   - Otherwise it calls `cookie_needs_write` (`sessions.py:233`), which returns true if the session was modified, or if it is permanent and `SESSION_REFRESH_EACH_REQUEST` is set.\n   - It then calls `get_expiration_time` (`sessions.py:~224`), then `make_signer(app).dumps(dict(session))` (`sessions.py:303`) to sign the payload.\n   - Finally it calls `response.set_cookie(...)` (`sessions.py:374`), which writes the `Set-Cookie` header, and adds `Vary: Cookie`.\n\nThe test client has its own copy of this step at `src/tessel/testing.py:177`.",
